==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ten-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|rétentif}}, from {{der|en|fro|retentif}}, from {{der|en|la-med|retentivus}}, from {{der|en|la|retentus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈtɛntɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-retentive.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having power to [[retain]].
#: {{ux|en|a soil that is highly '''retentive''' of rainwater}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|1|3|text=Nor airless dungeon, nor strong links of iron, Can be '''retentive''' to the strength of spirit.}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Max Carrados|passage=Mr Carlyle smiled his indulgence privately.<br>"My dear chap, you mustn't let your '''retentive''' memory of obscure happenings run away with you," he remarked wisely.}}
# {{lb|en|slang, [[apocope]]}} [[anal-retentive|Anal-retentive]].

